Approved local continuation B1–B4: **4/4 verified**. Those scoped counts do not
represent product completion percentages or closure of the wider R27 objective.

## Delivered and frozen

Implementation is confined to `v2/experiments/action_executor/r27/broker`.
Sealed original, retention and runtime sources/candidates/Completion/reviews remain
unchanged. No new micro-TIP, framework or changed product/dependency source was needed.

Broker-only physical I/O serves opaque logical Path/File ports without exported
storage paths or descriptors. Cached native `open`/`os.open` on those ports
reject before artifact I/O. Explicit bridges replace filesystem monkeypatching.
This is a pinned cooperative-producer boundary, not a hostile same-UID,
Python-introspection or universal OS sandbox. Unknown native writers remain DENY.

One logical **10 MiB** prewrite/no-refund counter charges complete packet records,
framing and every physical copy/overwrite attempt. Family/count, combined bytes
and the complete predicted manifest are admitted before destructive open.
Deletion never refunds; raw overwritten/deleted attempts and ordered tombstones
remain recoverable. Reserve **16,988B =340 closure +264 controls +16,384 metadata**;
the final **90B** manifest-binding record is admitted before manifest I/O.
No truncation, read-chunk record splitting or digest replacement manufactures PASS.

Local domains: 32 file entries, 32 active ports, 32 active operations, 64 directories
and 64 deletion records. These do not prove the historical 63-file original campaign
fits. The budget is logical write accounting, not filesystem-block allocation.
Finish validates raw/native inventory and accounting before seal; recovery rejects
missing/extra/symlink/corrupt files. Immutable committed epochs and tamper rejection
are verified locally; power-cut durability and hostile races are not proved.

Real source bridges cover exact original journal/summary/write/print/oracle/final
blocks, the full pure signed fixture (five final files/six writes), actual audit
sink/restoration, safe original copy/literal expressions and R19 deadline/metadata
bodies. A legitimate source oracle SLA FAIL remains integrity-valid evidence;
unknown exceptions, serialization/storage/finalization faults remain INCOMPLETE.

The unchanged fixed child receives no broker root in argv/env/cwd or descriptors.
Concurrent bounded drains retain each entire stdout/stderr stream once at EOF.
One cleanup deadline is never renewed. All owned reader/waiter/operation joins
are attempted after faults; primary exception/cancellation identity is preserved.
An active-operation token prevents sealing before observed reap/join. Tests inspect
pending named owned tasks before event-loop shutdown, not after automatic runner
cancellation. Result metadata states Linux/group authority false and observed
reap/task/EOF state; unresolved ownership is HOLD, never inferred success.

The derived codec has exactly four approved root/identity substitutions, genuine
typed interface and AST/real-return conformance. **Its implementation body is not
strict-type/style body-audited**; old 246-error evidence remains historical.

Frozen identity is HEAD `0e88f48588dc3228f1ae9eca7a7597d96589af8b` plus dirty
source bytes, not a new commit or deployed runtime. Candidate includes **34 source
pins**, all ten owned Python/interface files. Binding has 139 direct pins and one
recursive anchor.

