Two actual pytest configuration warnings remain: plugin autoload is disabled while
the reused backend config names asyncio settings. These local async paths use
`asyncio.run`; zero skips. The separate 27 units use the explicit asyncio plugin.
This is not clean whole-backend health. The 1,600 fixed producer rows are synthetic
controls, not observed requests or an SLA measurement.

Before/after: **1,910 prior pins /14,510,687B; 2,010 total /15,420,190B**.
The prior graph includes the sealed runtime binding itself. Product204/tests192
inventories and digests, pyproject/uv.lock, all prior sealed candidates/reviews and
source bytes remain unchanged. Main independently reconstructed the graph rather
than relying only on the implementation's preservation helper.

## Preserved failures and cleanup

Core/peer failures, exact snapshots, initial format/type failures and the first
frozen candidate remain retained. Initial fourteen-PASS runs had wrapper exit1
because concurrent Builder/Main scratch snapshots differed; they are not claimed
wrapper PASS. Final verification is serial, with empty before/after scratch lists.

Main's actual backend-config check exposed 24 lint errors and seven formatting
differences despite earlier default-config checks. Repairs and refreeze preserve
those failed outputs and bytes; the final exact project-config checks pass.
A Main structural check wrongly assumed globally absent backend cache; that
failed assertion is retained. The unrelated old 92 MiB cache was preserved;
current commands use devnull/no-cache. No claim of globally empty caches is made.

Owned small test directories were automatically removed. No new dependency/venv,
whole-project copy, task build tree or Docker/SQL resource was created. No campaign,
external company-data/provider operation, Git write, rebuild, serving activation
or TIP-054.5 transition occurred. Existing unrelated dirty work remains intact.

## Next cohesive step

Complete **original-runtime broker routing and prerequisite validation within R27**:
the remaining shell/admin/migration/analysis/native emitters need actual admitted
ownership and source-compatible whole-record bounds; exact Linux child/group and
physical SQL lifecycle require separately authorized local runtime checks.
The existing 32-file domain must not be advertised as covering all historical output.

Only after those paths and prerequisites genuinely qualify should one exact
source-bound measurement grant be requested. Platform-audit approval is already
settled. No empty family receipt, synthetic grant JSON or earlier consumed allowance
authorizes effects. No further generic toy model or speculative latency tuning.

Preserve the unchanged 16 cells/1,600 requested observations, c1/10/25/50,
100 cases per operation, admission/submit/status/cancel, p95 500ms admission/
1,000ms others, zero errors, pool5+5/pre_ping, timeout0.9s, quotas5,000,
